H5500.definition:
a primitive root;
to sweep away
KJV: scrape.

H5501.definition:
from H5500 (סָחָה);
refuse (as swept off)
KJV: offscouring.

H5502.definition:
a primitive root;
to scrape off
KJV: sweep (away).

H5503.definition:
a primitive root;
to travel round (specifically as a pedlar); intensively, to palpitate
KJV: go about, merchant(-man), occupy with, pant, trade, traffick.

H5504.definition:
from H5503 (סָחַר);
profit (from trade)
KJV: merchandise.

H5505.definition:
from H5503 (סָחַר);
an emporium; abstractly, profit (from trade)
KJV: mart, merchandise.

H5507.definition:
properly, active participle feminine of H5503 (סָחַר);
something surrounding the person, i.e. a shield
KJV: buckler.

H5508.definition:
similar to H5507 (סֹחֵרָה);
probably a (black) tile (or tessara) forlaying borders with
KJV: black marble.

H5509.definition:
or סוּג; (Ezekiel 22:18), from H5472 (סוּג) in the sense of refuse;
scoria
KJV: dross.

H5510.definition:
probably of Persian origin;
Sivan, the third Hebrew month
KJV: Sivan.

H5511.definition:
or סִיחֹן; from the same as H5477 (סוּחַ); tempestuous;
Sichon, an Amoritish king
KJV: Sihon.

H5512.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Sin the name of an Egyptian town and (probably) desert adjoining
KJV: Sin.

H5513.definition:
from an otherwise unknown name of a man;
a Sinite, or descendant of one of the sons of Canaan
KJV: Sinite.

H5514.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Sinai, mountain of Arabia
KJV: Sinai.

H5515.definition:
plural of an otherwise unknown name;
Sinim, a distant Oriental region
KJV: Sinim.

H5516.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Sisera, the name of a Canaanitish king and of one of the Nethinim
KJV: Sisera.

H5517.definition:
or סִיעֲהָא; from an unused root meaning to converse; congregation;
Sia or Siaha, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Sia, Siaha.

H5518.definition:
or (feminine) סִירָה; or סִרָה; (Jeremiah 52:18), from a primitive root meaning to boil up;
a pot; also a thorn (as springing up rapidly); by implication, a hook
KJV: caldron, fishhook, pan, (wash-)pot, thorn.

H5519.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ);
properly, a thicket of men, i.e. a crowd
KJV: multitude.

H5520.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ);
a hut (as of entwined boughs); also a lair
KJV: covert, den, pavilion, tabernacle.

H5521.definition:
feminine of H5520 (סֹךְ);
a hut or lair
KJV: booth, cottage, covert, pavilion, tabernacle, tent.

H5522.definition:
feminine of H5519 (סָךְ);
an (idolatrous) booth
KJV: tabernacle.

H5523.definition:
or סֻכֹּת; plural of H5521 (סֻכָּה); booths;
Succoth, the name of a place in Egypt and of three in Palestine
KJV: Succoth.

H5524.definition:
from H5523 (סֻכּוֹת) and the (irregular) plural of H1323 (בַּת);
booths of (the) daughters; brothels, i.e. idoalatrous tents forimpure purpose
KJV: Succothbenoth.

H5525.definition:
patrial from an unknown name (perhaps H5520 (סֹךְ));
a Sukkite, or inhabitant of some place near Egypt (i.e. hut-dwellers)
KJV: Sukkiims.

H5526.definition:
or שָׂכַךְ; (Exodus 33:22), a primitive root;
properly, to entwine as ascreen; by implication, to fence in, cover over, (figuratively) protect
KJV: cover, defence, defend, hedge in, join together, set, shut up.

H5527.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ); inclosure;
Secacah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Secacah.

H5528.definition:
for H3688 (כָּסַל);
to be silly
KJV: do (make, play the, turn into) fool(-ish, -ishly, -ishness).

H5529.definition:
from H5528 (סָכַל);
silliness; concretely and collectively, dolts
KJV: folly.

H5530.definition:
from H5528 (סָכַל);
silly
KJV: fool(-ish), sottish.

H5531.definition:
or שִׂכְלוּת; (Ecclesiastes 1:17), from H5528 (סָכַל);
silliness
KJV: folly, foolishness.

H5532.definition:
a primitive root;
to be familiar with; by implication, to minister to, be serviceable to, be customary
KJV: acquaint (self), be advantage, [idiom] ever, (be, (un-)) profit(-able), treasurer, be wont.

H5533.definition:
probably a denominative from H7915 (שַׂכִּין);
properly, to cut, i.e. damage; also to grow (causatively, make) poor
KJV: endanger, impoverish.

H5534.definition:
a primitive root;
to shut up; by implication, to surrender
KJV: stop, give over. See also H5462 (סָגַר), H7936 (שָׂכַר).

H5535.definition:
a primitive root to be silent;
by implication, to observe quietly
KJV: take heed.

H5536.definition:
from H5549 (סָלַל);
properly, a willow twig (as pendulous), i.e. an osier; but only as woven into abasket
KJV: basket.

H5537.definition:
a primitive root;
to suspend in a balance, i.e. weigh
KJV: compare.

H5538.definition:
from H5549 (סָלַל); an embankment;
Silla, a place in Jerusalem
KJV: Silla.

H5539.definition:
a primitive root;
probably to leap (with joy), i.e. exult
KJV: harden self.

H5540.definition:
from H5539 (סָלַד); exultation;
Seled, an Israelite
KJV: Seled.

H5541.definition:
a primitive root;
to hang up, i.e. weigh, or (figuratively) contemn
KJV: tread down (under foot), value.

H5542.definition:
from H5541 (סָלָה);
suspension (of music), i.e. pause
KJV: Selah.

H5543.definition:
or סַלּוּא; or סָלוּא; or סַלַּי; from H5541 (סָלָה); weighed;
Sallu or Sallai, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Sallai, Sallu, Salu.

H5544.definition:
or סַלּוֹן; from H5541 (סָלָה);
a prickle (as if pendulous)
KJV: brier, thorn.

H5545.definition:
a primitive root;
to forgive
KJV: forgive, pardon, spare.

H5546.definition:
from H5545 (סָלַח);
placable
KJV: ready to forgive.

H5547.definition:
from H5545 (סָלַח);
pardon
KJV: forgiveness, pardon.

H5548.definition:
from an unused root. meaning to walk; walking;
Salcah, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Salcah, Salchah.

H5549.definition:
a primitive root;
to mound up (especially a turnpike); figurative, to exalt; reflexively, to oppose (as by a dam)
KJV: cast up, exalt (self), extol, make plain, raise up.

H5550.definition:
or סוֹלְלָה; active participle feminine of H5549 (סָלַל), but used passively;
a military mound, i.e. rampart of besiegers
KJV: bank, mount.

H5551.definition:
from H5549 (סָלַל);
a stair-case
KJV: ladder.

H5552.definition:
from H5541 (סָלָה);
a twig (as pendulous)
KJV: basket.

H5553.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be lofty;
a craggy rock, literally or figuratively (a fortress)
KJV: (ragged) rock, stone(-ny), strong hold.

H5554.definition:
the same as H5553 (סֶלַע);
Sela, the rock-city of Idumaea
KJV: rock, Sela(-h).

H5555.definition:
from H5553 (סֶלַע) and the plural of H4256 (מַחֲלֹקֶת) with the article interposed; rock of the divisions;
Sela-ham-Machlekoth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Sela-hammalekoth.

H5556.definition:
apparently from the same as H5553 (סֶלַע) in the sense of crushing as with a rock, i.e. consuming;
a kind of locust (from its destructiveness)
KJV: bald locust.

H5557.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to wrench, i.e. (figuratively) to subvert
KJV: overthrow, pervert.

H5558.definition:
from H5557 (סָלַף);
distortion, i.e. (figuratively) viciousness
KJV: perverseness.

H5559.definition:
(Aramaic) a primitive root;
to ascend
KJV: come (up).

H5560.definition:
from an unused root meaning to strip;
flour (as chipped off)
KJV: (fine) flour, meal.

H5561.definition:
from an unused root meaning to smell sweet;
an aroma
KJV: sweet (spice).

H5562.definition:
of foreign origin;
Samgar-Nebo, a Babylonian general
KJV: Samgar-nebo.

H5563.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a vine blossom; used also adverbially, abloom
KJV: tender grape.

H5564.definition:
a primitive root;
to prop (literally or figuratively); reflexively, to lean upon or take hold of (in a favorable or unfavorable sense)
KJV: bear up, establish, (up-) hold, lay, lean, lie hard, put, rest self, set self, stand fast, stay (self), sustain.

H5565.definition:
from H5564 (סָמַךְ) and H3050 (יָהּ); supported of Jah;
Semakjah, an Israelite
KJV: Semachiah.

H5566.definition:
or סֵמֶל; from an unused root meaning to resemble;
a likeness
KJV: figure, idol, image.

H5567.definition:
a primitive root;
to designate
KJV: appointed.

H5568.definition:
a primitive root;
to be erect, i.e. bristle as hair
KJV: stand up, tremble.

H5569.definition:
from H5568 (סָמַר);
bristling, i.e. shaggy
KJV: rough.

H5570.definition:
from an unused root meaning to prick; thorny;
Senaah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Senaah, Hassenaah (with the article).

H5571.definition:
of foreign origin;
Sanballat, a Persian satrap of Samaria
KJV: Sanballat.

H5572.definition:
from an unused root meaning to prick;
a bramble
KJV: bush.

H5573.definition:
the same as H5572 (סְנֶה); thorn;
Seneh, a crag in Palestine
KJV: Seneh.

H5574.definition:
or סְנֻאָה from the same as H5570 (סְנָאָה);
pointed; (used with the article as a proper name) Senuah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Hasenuah (including the art), Senuah.

H5575.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
(in plural) blindness
KJV: blindness.

H5576.definition:
of foreign origin;
Sancherib, an Assyrian king
KJV: Sennacherib.

H5577.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be pointed;
a twig (as tapering)
KJV: bough.

H5578.definition:
feminine of a form of H5577 (סַנְסִן); a bough;
Sansannah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Sansannah.

H5579.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a fin (collectively)
KJV: fins.

H5580.definition:
from the same as H5483 (סוּס);
a moth (from the agility of the fly)
KJV: moth.

H5581.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Sismai, an Israelite
KJV: Sisamai.

H5582.definition:
a primitive root;
to suport (mostly figurative)
KJV: comfort, establish, hold up, refresh self, strengthen, be upholden.

H5583.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5582 (סָעַד);
to aid
KJV: helping.

H5584.definition:
a primitive root;
to rush
KJV: storm.

H5585.definition:
from H5586 (סָעַף);
a fissure (of rocks); also a bough (as subdivided)
KJV: (outmost) branch, clift, top.

H5587.definition:
or שָׂעִף; from H5586 (סָעַף);
divided (in mind), i.e. (abstractly) a sentiment
KJV: opinion.

H5588.definition:
from H5586 (סָעַף);
divided (in mind), i.e. (concretely) a skeptic
KJV: thought.

H5589.definition:
feminine of H5585 (סָעִיף);
a twig
KJV: bough, branch. Compare H5634 (סַרְעַפָּה).

H5590.definition:
a primitive root;
to rush upon; by implication, to toss (transitive or intransitive, literal or figurative)
KJV: be (toss with) tempest(-uous), be sore, troubled, come out as a (drive with the, scatter with a) whirlwind.

H5591.definition:
or (feminine) סְעָרָה; from H5590 (סָעַר);
a hurricane
KJV: storm(-y), tempest, whirlwind.

H5592.definition:
from H5605 (סָפַף), in its original sense of containing;
a vestibule (as a limit); also a dish (for holding blood or wine)
KJV: bason, bowl, cup, door (post), gate, post, threshold.

H5593.definition:
the same as H5592 (סַף);
Saph, a Philistine
KJV: Saph. Compare H5598 (סִפַּי).

H5594.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to tear the hair and beat the breasts (as Orientals do in grief); generally to lament; by implication, to wail
KJV: lament, mourn(-er), wail.

H5595.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to scrape (literally, to shave; but usually figuratively) together (i.e. to accumulate or increase) or away (i.e. to scatter, remove, or ruin; intransitively, to perish)
KJV: add, augment, consume, destroy, heap, join, perish, put.

H5596.definition:
or שָׂפַח; (Isaiah 3:17), a primitive root;
properly, to scrape out, but in certain peculiar senses (of removal or association)
KJV: abiding, gather together, cleave, smite with the scab.

H5597.definition:
from H5596 (סָפַח);
the mange (as making the hair fall off)
KJV: scab.

H5598.definition:
from H5592 (סַף); bason-like;
Sippai, a Philistine
KJV: Sippai. Compare H5593 (סַף).

H5599.definition:
from H5596 (סָפַח);
something (spontaneously) falling off, i.e. a self-sown crop; figuratively, a freshet
KJV: (such) things as (which) grow (of themselves), which groweth of its own accord (itself).
